Z||000013||DRH||12-11-2001||05:51 PM||||I don't have a digital camera or scanner so I can't help you on pics. <P>From looking at mine, I believe the smaller holes are oil supply and the larger ones are return. <P>There's an aluminum cover plate that bolts over the center. It has passages to route oil from the round hole in the center toward the front to the two small holes that line up with the small holes to feed oil to the head. The cover plate also has a breather tube that lines up with the rectangular hole toward the front.<P>The intake bolts just to the heads. It doesn't touch the block at all. <P>You might be able to get oil to the head by tapping the oil feed in the head to take a high pressure line. It looks like your block may have a plug in the oil passage that could be used for a source if it provides enough volume. The oval shaped return might be a little more challenging, but at least it's no pressure.  You'll still need to seal off the valley area in your block somehow. Also, don't forget you'll need to seal the oil passages to the lifter holes somehow. <P>Probably not impossible... Definitely a challenge!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||1
